actor "Finder" as Actor
participant "Conversation Custody Transfer" as Page
participant "Claims API" as API
participant "Claim Custody Service" as Service
participant "custody_requests" as Table <<entity>>

Actor -> Page: 1: Open Request transfer to staff custody
activate Page
Page -> API: 2: POST /api/claims/:id/verification/decision (ESCALATE_TO_CUSTODY)
activate API
API -> API: 3: Validate access session, role and input
alt Valid request
API -> Service: 4: Request transfer to staff custody
activate Service
Service -> Service: 5: Require actual Finder, explicit reason and active intake point
Service -> Service: 6: Lock eligible owned FOUND OR exact approved photo-backed LOST room
alt Physical source or consumed contact photo eligible
Service -> Table: 7: INSERT PENDING exact-source custody request or stable replay
activate Table
Table --> Service: 8: Custody request
deactivate Table
Service -> Service: 9: For no-FOUND: keep physical post_id NULL; bind claim/room/Finder
Service -> Service: 10: Preserve claim verification; write audit/notifications and commit
Service --> API: 11: Custody transfer request
API --> Page: 12: HTTP 200: Custody transfer request
Page --> Actor: 13: Show authorized result
else Source/room/photo invalid or already in custody
Service --> API: 7.1: Custody cannot be queued for this context
API --> Page: 7.2: HTTP 409
Page --> Actor: 7.3: Display error; do not report success
end
deactivate Service
else Invalid input, missing session or insufficient role
API --> Page: 4.1: HTTP 422 / 401 / 403 (429 only if rate-limited)
Page --> Actor: 4.2: Show appropriate error; retain form/draft
end
deactivate API
deactivate Page

legend left
Scope: This depicts the chat route; owned FOUND also has staff/custody-requests creation. No FOUND
is required for approved direct LOST contact. Queueing does not physically receive property or
verify ownership.
